    "title": "2 Rocky River High School baseball coaches resign after Myrtle Beach 'incident' - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jordan Unger ,\n2 hours ago\nROCKY RIVER, Ohio (WJW) – The Rocky River High School baseball team will finish their season with a new coach.\nA message sent to parents said head coach Ed Piazza and and assistant coach Michael Harper have resigned after an incident that took place over the weekend.\nPHOTOS: Storms sweep through NE Ohio, causing wind, hail damage School officials did not say what that incident was, but they said it happened in Myrtle Beach and involved members of the baseball team.\nAssistant coach Craig Moro will take over as head coach for the remainder of the season.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Fox 8 Cleveland WJW.\n1",
    "summary": "ROCKY RIVER, Ohio (WJW) – The Rocky River High School baseball team will finish their season with a new coach. A message sent to parents said head coach Ed Piazza and and assistant coach Michael Harper have resigned after an incident that took place over the weekend. PHOTOS: Storms sweep through NE Ohio, causing wind, hail damage School officials did not say what that incident was, but they said it happened in Myrtle Beach and involved members of the baseball team. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
